From e89002e43ad38099052ec7326656f8c48c1cb1d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lou Viannay <lou.viannay@octavesolution.com>
Date: Sun, 29 Mar 2026 14:04:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] sound/dts: add Allwinner H616/H618 AHUB driver for HDMI
 audio
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

New driver sun50i-ahub.c implements the Audio Hub (AHUB) APBIF0→I2S1
path required for HDMI audio on H616/H618. The AHUB has no standalone
I2S controllers; audio must be routed through the crossbar: DMA writes
to APBIF0 TX FIFO, which feeds I2S port 1 (hardwired to DW-HDMI I2S
input).

- sound/soc/sunxi/sun50i-ahub.c: new minimal driver
  - Handles clocks (audio-hub, bus-audio-hub) and CCU reset
  - Routes APBIF_TXDIF0 → I2S1 via RXCONT register
  - I2S1 in master mode (drives BCLK/LRCK at 64×fs for DW-HDMI)
  - hw_params configures word size, BCLKDIV, channel count
  - trigger enables/disables APBIF0 TX DRQ and I2S1 TXEN
  - Uses devm_snd_dmaengine_pcm_register (DMA port 3 for APBIF0 TX)
- sun50i-h616.dtsi: add ahub@5097000 node (disabled by default)
- sun50i-h618-longanpi-3h.dts: enable ahub, add simple-audio-card
  connecting ahub (CPU DAI) to hdmi (dw-hdmi-i2s-audio codec)
- Kconfig/Makefile: SND_SUN50I_AHUB config
- longanpi_3h_defconfig: CONFIG_SND_SUN50I_AHUB=m

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
